mage`\n  - `generateVideo()` — calls `POST /inference/video`\n  - `enhanceImage()` — calls `POST /inference/enhance`\n  - `listModels()` — calls `GET /inference/models`\n\n---\n\n## 4. Configuration Files and API Key Storage\n\n### Backend Environment Variables (`/home/sameer/hash-shit/8x/inference/`)\n\n- **`config.py`** — Loads settings from `.env` using Pydantic Settings:\n  - `POLLINATIONS_BASE_URL` (default: `https://image.pollinations.ai`)\n  - `POLLINATIONS_API_KEY` (optional)\n  - `DEFAULT_IMAGE_MODEL=flux`\n  - `DEFAULT_VIDEO_MODEL` (empty — no default set)\n  - `DEFAULT_TEXT_MODEL` (empty)\n  - `DEFAULT_ENHANCE_MODEL` (empty)\n  - `CORS_ORIGINS`\n  - `REQUEST_TIMEOUT`, `MAX_IMAGE_WIDTH`, etc.\n\n- **`.env.example`** — Template showing expected env vars\n\n### Frontend Environment Variables (`/home/sameer/hash-shit/8x/app/.env`)\n\n- `INFERENCE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000`\n- `INFERENCE_API_KEY=` (empty)\n- Database URL, JWT secret, SMTP, Stripe keys, R2 credentials\n\n### Database Schema (Prisma)\n\n- **`/home/sameer/hash-shit/8x/app/prisma/schema.prisma`** — `ModelConfig` table stores model metadata:\n  ```prisma\n  model ModelConfig {\n    id          String\n    name        String   @unique      // e.g., \"flux\", \"json2video\"\n    displayName String\n    type        String                // \"image\" | \"video\" | \"enhance\"\n    provider    String                // \"pollinations\" | \"future_provider\"\n    creditCost  Int\n    config      Json                  // Provider-specific defaults\n    active      Boolean\n  }\n  ```\n\n  To add a JSON2Video model, you would insert a row with `type: \"video\"`, `provider: \"json2video\"` (or whatever you name it), and the relevant config JSON.\n\n---\n\n## Summary for Implementation\n\nTo implement a JSON2Video feature, you would need to:\n\n1. **Create a new provider** in `/home/sameer/hash-shit/8x/inference/providers/` (e.g., `json2video.py`) that:\n   - Subclasses `BaseProvider`\n   - Sets `task_type = \"video\"`\n   - Defines `request_model = VideoGenerationRequest`\n   - Defines `response_model = VideoGenerationResponse`\n   - Implements `generate()` and `format_output()` to call the JSON2Video API\n   - Adds the provider to `providers/registry.py`\n\n2. **Add API keys** to `inference/config.py` and `inference/.env.example` for the JSON2Video service.\n\n3. **Add a ModelConfig** entry in the database with `type: \"video\"`, `provider: \"json2video\"`, etc.\n\n4. **No frontend changes** are strictly necessary — the UI and API routes already support video. You may want to update the generate page to show video-specific controls (duration, fps) when the video tab is active.\n\nThe codebase is well-structured and the video pipeline is already wired up end-to-end; it just needs an actual video provider implementation.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>1995</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>33</tool_uses><duration_ms>106190</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}

