{"session_id":"fbd7b413-a099-4250-8ee4-d7a8e7555d56","transcript_path":"/home/sameer/.claude/projects/-home-sameer-hash-shit-8x/fbd7b413-a099-4250-8ee4-d7a8e7555d56.jsonl","cwd":"/home/sameer/hash-shit/8x","prompt_id":"b611a03c-10d8-4ec1-8abd-b4ab46641507","permission_mode":"default","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"Stop","stop_hook_active":false,"last_assistant_message":"`INFERENCE_API_KEY` is a **pass-through API key** for the upstream providers (Pollinations.ai, JSON2Video), not a key for the relay itself.\n\nHere's how it flows:\n\n1. **App** (`/app/config/inference.ts`) sends `X-API-Key: <INFERENCE_API_KEY>` to `http://localhost:8000`\n2. **Inference relay** (`/inference/routes/image.py`) receives it via the `X-API-Key` header\n3. **Relay forwards it** to the actual provider (e.g., Pollinations.ai or JSON2Video)\n\nSo if you set `INFERENCE_API_KEY=your-pollinations-key`, your images get generated via your Pollinations account. If you leave it blank, the relay falls back to its own defaults (`POLLINATIONS_API_KEY` / `JSON2VIDEO_API_KEY` from the inference `.env`).\n\n### When do you need it?\n\n| Scenario | What to do |\n|----------|-----------|\n| **Just testing locally** | Leave it blank — the relay has its own defaults |\n| **Using your own Pollinations account** | Set `INFERENCE_API_KEY` to your Pollinations API key |\n| **Private generation** | Pollinations requires a key for `private: true` requests |\n| **JSON2Video** | JSON2Video requires a key entirely (no free tier) |\n\n### The relay's own defaults\n\nIn `/inference/.env`:\n```bash\nPOLLINATIONS_API_KEY=your_api_key_here   # relay's fallback for pollinations\nJSON2VIDEO_API_KEY=your_key_here           # relay's fallback for json2video\n```\n\nSo the relay supports **two ways** to pass provider keys:\n- **App-level**: `INFERENCE_API_KEY` in `/app/.env` (sent per-request)\n- **Relay-level**: `POLLINATIONS_API_KEY` / `JSON2VIDEO_API_KEY` in `/inference/.env` (relay fallback)\n\nIf you set both, the app-level key **wins** because it overrides the relay's default.\n\n---\n\n**Bottom line:** For local development, you can leave `INFERENCE_API_KEY` empty. For production or if you want to track usage under your own accounts, set it to your provider's key.","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}

